# Build output. `target/` alone is 19 GB against 2.3 MB of source.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Frontend
/ui/node_modules/
/ui/dist/
/ui/.vite/
/ui/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tauri generates these into the app crate at build time.
/crates/cide-app/gen/

# Editor and tool state that is per-machine, not per-project.
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Local permission grants and machine-specific settings. `.claude/settings.json`
# would be shared configuration and is deliberately not ignored; this file is not.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent worktrees live inside the repo. Without this, a single `git add -A` during a
# parallel run commits six complete copies of the source tree — and git happily lets you.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Agent worktrees, again: `.cide/worktrees/` is one full checkout per agent, and the
# argument three lines up applies unchanged.
/.cide/worktrees/

# The rest of `.cide/` is committed on purpose. This line used to read `/.cide/`, on the
# premise that the directory held "runtime state cide itself writes" — it never did:
# workspace.json and everything like it live in $XDG_STATE_HOME/cide. `.cide/config.json`,
# `.cide/agents/*.md` and `.cide/tasks.json` are shared project configuration, hand-edited
# and reviewed in diffs, so this repository has to be able to commit its own.

# Run logs, wherever they land. (This line kept the heading it used to share.)
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/NOTES.md
